rst  saw a narrative I could shape I learned  the Jedi Code from master Vande are my  very own Yoda there is no death berries  divorce I built my own lightsaber and  learn from and grew close to Bastila I  began to understand the force its power  and its fragility I put that to the test  when I had to decide the fate of Juhani  the Cathar Jedi on the brink of falling  to the dark side I thank you master Jedi  I will return special  I shall submit myself to their judgement  and hope you will forgive me player  agency permeated my trek across the  galaxy it's great that you could fully  embrace the dark side but I chose the  light the main objectives were always  the same find the star map to find and  destroy the star Forge but how I  accomplished this and the decisions I  made along the way are what captivated  me when I landed on Kashuk I knew I was  going to drive out the zurka corporation  for slaving wookies but who was I going  to help run things afterward solve our  got my back so I got his if you got to  know him and his family you could  understand what keep politics so the  first time I saw Chewbacca in the movies  it's as if I knew his ancestors and  understood the struggles that took place  on Kashuk well before his time stepping  onto the rough sands of Tatooine as my  own Jedi thousands of years before Luke  Skywalker I almost felt the heat of the  planets to sun's beating down on me when  I land on manaan I just stopped to look  around soak in the vastness of the ocean  and the tranquility of Auto City I  learned about the shiny cell cat folk  but also had to decide the future of  their environment but it wasn't until  Korriban a barren desolate planet that  it truly understood the dark side  undercover as a student at their academy  I saw their ways  savage ruthless but their will fickle as  I walk through the valley of the Dark  Lord's there stood monuments of the past  sit rulers  all this time I had a ragtag crew of  misfits unique in their own way  the comically violent droid HK 47 a  prideful and aggressive Mandalorian and  kandra's the scrappy twi'lek mission veo  the nagging ly virtuous cars and t3m for  a spiritual predecessor to r2d2 just the  name a few these are just a few of the  memories I have leaving my mark in  galactic history but nothing is more  burnt into my memory than the moments on  the Leviathan my relatively calm quest  for the star maps and the star Forge  reached a turning point and facing Darth  Malak for the first time many truths  were unveiled why did I have all these  visions of exactly where I needed to go  where all the star maps were why did I  share the seemingly curious yet strong  bond with past alone and why did I  become such a powerful Jedi in such a  short period of time there's one answer  I was Darth Revan  and in that moment my understanding of  who my character was why the story even  existed in the first place was a sort of  limbo now the game walked me back  through the trail of breadcrumbs they  left that hinted at my character's true  identity but I still had so many  unanswered questions it's regarded as  one of the greatest plot twists in  gaming history but it was hardly the end  of the story  Basque Allah sacrificed herself to hold  off Malik but it would come back to  haunt us as we crash-landed on the  unknown planet inhabited by the ancient  rocket aah  but just as she saved reven me from the  dark side I too had the chance to bring  her back your brave mister was a fool  but you were also right the dark side is  not totally consumed me I cannot raise  my blade against you everything led to  the Battle of the star Forge the  relentless war factory that it pump out  endless warships and crushed the  Republic but my bond with Vassalo was  strong enough she could turn her  all-powerful battle meditation against  the Sith and turned the tide then I  would finally square up with Malik one  on one and just as I saw later in the  movies the light prevailed but not  without tragic losses along the way and  in the end  as the darkness takes me  Knights of the Old Republic is a  magnificent game and a beautiful Star  Wars story but what I realize is that  despite having the choice between dark  and light the journey was anything but  black-and-white I went in without much  knowledge but I came out enraptured by  this universe my love for Knights of the  Old Republic made a seamless transition  to the franchise as a whole  I saw the Millennium Falcon and thought  of the ebon Hawk I heard yo to speak and  remembered the wise words of master van  der I saw the death star and was  reminded as a star Forge and so when I  watched Leia Organa and Luke Skywalker  lead a rebellion against the Empire in  the back of my mind was bachelor Shawn  and revin and the lives they led 4,000  years ago as Star Wars enters another  era and reaches a different generation a  new foundation is built for new fans  their first memories will probably be of  an older Luke han and Leia with rey and  finn taking the fight to kylo Ren and  that's just as valid as how I was  invested in being revin hopping from  planet to planet trying to leave my mark  across the galaxy and ultimately defeat  Darth Malak  and the Sith Empire Knights of the Old  Republic gave me Star Wars and the  excitement to be a fan of this franchise  it's something I'll always cherish  wherever you go you will be recognized  as the saviors of the galaxy the heroes  fire age  but you must remain ever-vigilant for  one day you may be called upon yet again  to defend the glory of the Republic  against the jeers guitar side is the  destiny of the Jedi  [Music]  I am only one of many who have a story  to tell so please share how you fell in  love with Star Wars in the comments  below and my friends and colleagues here  at GameSpot also have stories to tell so  please subscribe to our channel thanks  for watching  [Music]
 

